   "text": "I read the structure as a PROTAC with a covalent KRAS G12C-type warhead joined through a PEG linker to a VHL ligand, and wrote the SMILES in those three parts.\n\n**Warhead (left side).**\n- A quinazoline core carries an acryloyl-piperazine at C4.\n- It has a 2-NH substituent, an 8-fluoro group, a 6-chloro group, and a 3-hydroxynaphthalen-1-yl group at C7.\n\n**Linker.**\n- The 2-NH is attached to \u2013CH2CH2C(=O)N(CH3)\u2013.\n- Next comes a chain of five ethylene-oxy units: N\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH. I counted five ether oxygens along the drawn chain.\n\n**VHL ligand (right side).**\n- The linker amide NH connects to tert-leucine, then to 4-hydroxyproline, then to an (S)-1-[4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)phenyl]ethylamine.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I took the stereocentres to match the standard VHL ligand configuration: tert-leucine S, hydroxyproline (2S,4R) and the methylbenzylamine carbon S. I wrote the chirality tags from that convention, adjusted for atom order in my SMILES, rather than re-deriving each wedge from the drawing.\n\nSMILES: C=CC(=O)N1CCN(CC1)c1nc(NCCC(=O)N(C)CCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N2C[C@H](O)C[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H](C)c2ccc(cc2)-c2scnc2C)nc2c(F)c(c(Cl)cc12)-c1cc(O)cc2ccccc12"
  }
